          <msContents>
            <summary>Herbal in Italian. With an added collection of alchemical receipts and iatro-chemical remedies: also notes on conception, pregnancy, and astrology by Luigi Dardano. Written by various hands. Twelve leaves containing the alchemical receipts, etc. have been bound in between fol. 31 and fol. 32. There are 56 ll. containing water-colour drawings of medicinal plants. These are of a crude type, in the style of the early printed herbals: some have grotesque heads and faces included in the design. Each has a short description in Italian. The Index is on fol. 31 and fol. 32: it contains entries for the missing ff. 61, 62. Dardano's work is found on the versos of ff. 35-38, 40, 41, 43: at the end (fol. 43v) is a note 'Tutta l'antedetta dottrina e di Luigi Dardano Gran Canceliero del Senato Vinitiano'.</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">Italian</textLang>
            <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_337_1">
              <author/>
              <title type="original">Herbals: 16th cent.</title>
              <title type="standard"/>
              <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">Italian</textLang>
              <filiation/>
            </msItem>
          </msContents>
